    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/8/48899.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 20,
    "turn_text": "That whole thing. And so what we want to do is get rid of the mandates in medicine. That's what you want to do. You want to get rid of it. Because my position is that we even talked about this today on our program. But I'm not doing this program to get rid of vaccines. That isn't it. What I want is a choice on the vaccine. I took the polio vaccine back when I was in college. And that wasn't even an issue. It wasn't a major decision. But the decision should be made by the individual himself, and that's what medicine is about. I talk a lot about free-market medicine and that the doctor-patient relationship is what you want to restore, because the other words that I like to use as volunteerism. Well, that sounds very good. If you come to my house, if I know you and want you to come in, I open the door and you voluntarily come in. Voluntaryism can solve a lot of problems. All your associations should be voluntary, but that isn't the way they see it. You will do this and you will associate with this person and that person. And they control you by eliminating this whole concept of volunteerism. And that's the way it should be with vaccines. People who want the vaccines, they can take them. There should be no prohibition, but there should be no mandates either.",
