    "turn_text": "own choice. It's voluntary. You can't have one answer to that. You can't have one answer for medical care or social reasons or sexual reasons or anything. Everything has to be voluntary and both sides have to have an agreement. That's what all good economic policy deals with is they come together and there was a long time in history where it was thought in economic policy that one person benefit at the other person's injury, the other person's sacrificed. And it turned out where somebody figured out, no. Both sides agree, you know, I want the money and you want the substance and we volunteer, we make the exchange and both people win. And that's so much different than believing that somebody has to lose and somebody else wins in social things. That's the way it should be as well. And we should learn more often how to deal with other countries in that same fashion because we're imperfect and a lot of imperfections around the world. And there's no reason in the world why we should be dictating the answer to all their problems. And if we have a better system, if we have a free market system and we're doing very, very well, we can't use our thuggery to go around and invade our countries and say, you will be like us. What you want to do is persuade people and do it by setting an example and saying look at what you can have and that's a voluntary system and that's what we need and we could solve everything that's going wrong in these last two years especially could be solved by both sides agreeing that it should be voluntary and get rid of the authoritarian who think they're God themselves.",
