    "turn_text": "Yeah, I think one of the places I'm encouraged and I'd interested to hear your thoughts on this. We have a huge problem with censorship today. Uh, if the masters over at Twitter or Facebook or YouTube, who knows, I might get, I might get my third strike today because we talked, we dared talk about COVID, right? Um, and we dared talk about vaccines. We didn't even say anything negative. We just said we shouldn't be forcing them on people. I might, I might be done today. Who knows? Um, but alternative social media seems, and I don't even call it alternative anymore. Basically I refer to them as legacy. Social media and I think that that's something that that young people really excel at is all building these new platforms Some of them are being developed on blockchains, so they're immutable or they can't be censored They're censorship-proof because it's one thing to be able to come out in a court of public opinion and say this is the other side of the issue These are the things you didn't know. Did you know that like, I don't know the inventor of the mRNA technology says you should use some considerations before you use it because it really wasn't designed and used in mass this way. Like I'd say he's an expert and not be shut down because being shut down, it denies. See, I think it's two, it's two offenses. One, if it's me or you, it denies us the ability to speak. But the bigger offense is it denies anybody that wants to hear it. the ability to hear it. That's actually the larger offense and we need to be like really pounding on ways we can make sure that we don't have our voices silence, not for us, but for everybody speaking and for everybody listening.",
