    "turn_idx": 58,
    "turn_text": "But I do it because I enjoy it. I do it because I actually don't think that, you know, I studied, I do it, and I have the answer. It's something to me, we talked a little bit about in medicine, medicine is an ongoing operation to learn and expand your knowledge. And that's the way that I look at this, too, because there's a different issue every day. And how do you apply the principles of liberty to the different problems? So to me, And one thing I say to a crowd that I've spoken, because the interesting thing is, if I speak for an hour, the first 45 minutes is really, I lay it out there. You're going to be in big trouble, deficit exploding, and all that kind of stuff. The last 15 minutes I talk about the positive things, And that's interesting that a lot of people when they come up to me, and they say, I like to hear you speak because you're so optimistic. Well, yes, I am optimistic, but most of my speech was trying to wake you up. And I think it's information rather than saying that I'm being real pessimistic. But I think telling the truth is important. And then where I really believe that I am totally convinced of is if we want to live in a better system of government and have better conditions for everybody, you have to understand the basic principle of personal liberty and responsibility.",
